  "title": "The Teacup Lighthouse",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "miniature adventure",
  "premise": "A tiny sailor wants to guide a lost toy boat across a dark tabletop puddle, but reflections make three identical cup handles look like harbor entrances. The sailor rotates a patterned saucer under one cup, creating a distinctive moving reflection that the boat follows home.",
  "hook": "Three harbors. Only one is real.",
  "visible_action": "Boat circles reflected handles; saucer rotates; striped reflection sweeps the puddle; the boat follows the unique signal.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Distinctive signals can distinguish otherwise similar landmarks.",
  "gate": "Stylized tabletop reflections; do not present as maritime navigation guidance.",
